  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting wire is stretched by applying a deforming force, so that its diameter decreases to $40 \\%$ of original value. The percentage change in its resistance will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "83jks",
      "text": "$0.9 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "M5a0G",
      "text": "$0.12 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bCry3",
      "text": "$1.6 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7Vy0U",
      "text": "$0.5 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "On stretching, volume of wire remains constant.\nSo,\n$V=A l$ or $l=\\frac{V}{A}$\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\therefore & R=\\rho \\cdot \\frac{l}{A}=\\frac{\\rho V}{A^2}=\\frac{\\rho V}{\\frac{\\pi^2 D^4}{16}}=\\frac{16 \\rho V}{\\pi^2 D^4} \\\\\n\\therefore & \\frac{\\Delta R}{R}=-4 \\frac{\\Delta D}{D}=-4(-0.4)=1.6 \\%\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
